<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippine Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896–1898</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Philippine Revolution was the armed struggle against Spanish rule launched by the Katipunan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> in August 1896. After a truce in 1897 it revived in 1898 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, leading to the declaration of independence on 12 June 1898 and the First Philippine Republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> then ceded the islands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution.jpg" alt="Philippine Revolution" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Desconocido (pertenece a la misma sesión de fotos que File:Los defensores de Baler en Barcelona (septiembre de 1899, ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UltimosFilipinas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
